<title>NEW ZEALAND: Helicopter Line year profit falls 31 pct.</title>
<headline>Helicopter Line year profit falls 31 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 12.19 vs 17.74</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 27.7 vs 40.3</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				  8.0 vs same</p>
<p>    Total div for yr (cents)		15.0 vs same</p>
<p>    Turnover				   139.9 vs 90.9</p>
<p>    Abnormals				    nil vs 3.3 profit</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    21.48 vs 24.07</p>
<p>    Tax					    6.8 vs 6.9</p>
<p>    Equity earnings		   debit 1.31 vs 0.57 credit</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	  44.0 vs same</p>
<p>Dividend carries 3.94 cps imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date Nov 15</p>
<p>Reg date Nov 1</p>
<p>    Ex div   Nov 4</p>
<p>Note - The Helicopter Line Ltd is a tourism company, which plans to change its name to Tourism Holdings from October 1. The previous year's profit included a gain of $3.2 million from the sale of shares in Christchurch Casino.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
